<HelpTab>
    <HelpSection Title="Party Settings">
        <FluentText>
            <a href="/manage/parties/settings">Party Settings</a> is per location. Admins pick the <strong>Location</strong>;
            managers change the one they signed in to.
        </FluentText>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Timings</strong>: how long a party lasts, and how many minutes after arrival the children eat and play
                laser tag. These fill in the times when you book a party. Leave a time blank to leave that box empty. Press
                <strong>Save timings</strong> when you're done.</li>
            <li><strong>Hot food menu</strong>: the <strong>Meals</strong>, with their allergens, and the <strong>Sides</strong>
                offered with every meal.</li>
            <li><strong>Cold food menu</strong>: the <strong>Sandwiches</strong>, and the <strong>Other items in the box</strong>,
                which only appear in the allergy panel.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Party staffing">
        <FluentText>
            Under <strong>Party staffing</strong> on Party Settings, say how many extra staff each type of party needs.
            When you use <strong>Auto-build</strong> on the rota, it adds them to the shift each booked party falls in, on top
            of what that shift's template needs. They work the whole shift, for example 09:00 to 14:00 for a party at 10:00,
            and do the party as part of it. It needs Staff Scheduling to be switched on.
        </FluentText>
        <ol>
            <li>Select <strong>Add party staffing</strong>.</li>
            <li>Under <strong>For</strong>, pick a party type you've used on bookings, <strong>Another party type...</strong> to type
                one in, <strong>Any other party</strong> for every type that has no staffing of its own, or one of the
                <strong>Private hire</strong> kinds.</li>
            <li>Choose the <strong>Position</strong> and <strong>How many extra</strong>, then save.</li>
        </ol>
        <FluentText>
            Add one line per position, for example 2 Party Hosts and 1 Kitchen for "Lazer + Play". Types are matched to each
            booking's type ignoring capitals; private hires only use their own lines. Two bookings in the same shift add up.
            The extra people go to one shift: the one during the booking whose template already lists that position (so a
            hire's extra manager joins the late manager shift), otherwise the shift that covers most of the booking. On the rota the extra shift's note shows the shift and "Party: " with the type, never the child's name.
        </FluentText>
        <FluentText>
            If no shift template covers a party's time, Auto-build adds nobody for it and warns you, so you can add a template
            or staff it by hand.
        </FluentText>
        <FluentText>
            If a party is cancelled or moves to another shift after Auto-build, the next Auto-build takes off the party's
            draft shifts and adds new ones where needed. A shift you've already published is left alone, with a warning to change it yourself.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Printouts">
        <FluentText>
            <a href="/manage/parties/printouts">Printouts</a> lets you use your own artwork for the reserved table card, the free
            return voucher and the feedback form. These apply at every location in your company. Without artwork, Lanyard prints its standard design with
            your logo and colour.
        </FluentText>
        <ol>
            <li>Export your blank design, with the boxes left empty, as a PNG or JPEG, and upload it.</li>
            <li>Set the <strong>Printed size</strong> in millimetres and choose <strong>Handwritten</strong> or <strong>Standard</strong> lettering.</li>
            <li>Under <strong>Boxes</strong>, choose <strong>What goes here</strong> for each box and position it in millimetres from
                the artwork's top-left corner. The drawing shows where every box goes; click a box on it to edit that one.
                <strong>Add a box</strong> and <strong>Reset to default positions</strong> are underneath.</li>
            <li>The reserved table card starts as A5 landscape with one box across the middle for the child's name in capitals.
                You can add boxes for the arrival time, room or anything else on the list.</li>
            <li>For the voucher, set how many months it's valid for after the party (12 by default, up to 60).</li>
            <li>Press <strong>Save</strong>, then <strong>Preview saved version</strong> to print a sample.</li>
        </ol>
        <FluentText>
            To go back to Lanyard's own design, press <strong>Remove artwork (use the standard design)</strong>, then <strong>Save</strong>.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
